      "data": {
        "settings": {
          "id": "2",
          "title": "Grammar",
          "subtitle": "I Am Human",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": 1,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "He are my brother.",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "He is my brother.",
                    "correct": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "He am my brother.",
                    "correct": false
                  }
                ],
                "examples": [
                  "I am a man.",
                  "You are a student.",
                  "He is my friend.",
                  "She is a teacher."
                ],
                "description": "This week, you're continuing to use the verb \"to be\" (am, is, are), but now with personal pronouns like I, you, he, she to describe people and relationships.\n\nWe use these structures to talk about who someone is:",
                "questionText": "Which sentence is correct?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
            {
              "id": 2,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "He",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "I",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "You",
                    "correct": true
                  }
                ],
                "examples": [
                  "I am a student.",
                  "You are my friend.",
                  "He is a good boy.",
                  "She is my mom.",
                  "We are family.",
                  "They are neighbors."
                ],
                "description": "Here's how to match subject pronouns with the correct form of \"to be\":\n\n**Pronoun** | **Verb** | **Example**\nI | am | I am a student.\nYou | are | You are my friend.\nHe | is | He is a good boy.\nShe | is | She is my mom.\nWe | are | We are family.\nThey | are | They are neighbors.",
                "questionText": "Which pronoun goes with \"are\"?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
            {
              "id": 3,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "She'm",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "She're",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "She's",
                    "correct": true
                  }
                ],
                "sections": [
                  {
                    "name": "In English, we often use contractions when speaking casually. Here's how:",
                    "examples": [
                      "I am → I'm",
                      "You are → You're",
                      "He is → He's",
                      "She is → She's",
                      "We are → We're",
                      "They are → They're"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "name": "Examples:",
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm happy.",
                      "She's kind.",
                      "You're amazing."
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "questionText": "What is the contraction of \"She is\"?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
            {
              "id": 4,
              "type": "listen_only",
              "content": {
