          "subtitle": "My Day",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": 1,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "I eat breakfast.",
                    "correct": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "I eats breakfast.",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "I am eat breakfast.",
                    "correct": false
                  }
                ],
                "examples": [
                  "I eat breakfast.",
                  "I wake up early.",
                  "I go to work."
                ],
                "description": "This week we focus on using **verbs to describe daily actions**, especially in the morning and afternoon. You'll continue using **\"to be\"** and add **action verbs** like eat, wake up, and go.",
                "questionText": "Which sentence is correct?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
            {
              "id": 2,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "She eat toast.",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "She eats toast.",
                    "correct": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "She eating toast.",
                    "correct": false
                  }
                ],
                "examples": [
                  "I wake up early.",
                  "You take a shower.",
                  "He eats toast for breakfast.",
                  "She drinks juice.",
                  "We cook eggs in the morning.",
                  "They go to work on time."
                ],
                "description": "Here are verbs in simple present form for routines:\n\n**Subject** | **Verb Example** | **Complete Sentence**\nI | wake up | I wake up early.\nYou | take | You take a shower.\nHe | eats | He eats toast for breakfast.\nShe | drinks | She drinks juice.\nWe | cook | We cook eggs in the morning.\nThey | go | They go to work on time.",
                "questionText": "Which is correct for \"she\"?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
            {
              "id": 3,
              "type": "choose_text_from_audio",
              "content": {
                "options": [
                  {
                    "text": "He go to work.",
                    "correct": false
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "He goes to work.",
                    "correct": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "He going to work.",
                    "correct": false
                  }
                ],
                "sections": [
                  {
                    "name": "In the **present tense**, when the subject is **he, she, or it**, you usually add **-s** to the verb:",
                    "examples": [
                      "He eats",
                      "She drinks",
                      "It starts"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "name": "Also:",
                    "examples": [
                      "Go → Goes",
                      "Do → Does",
                      "Have → Has"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "name": "Examples:",
                    "examples": [
                      "He eats breakfast.",
                      "She drinks coffee.",
                      "It starts at 8 AM.",
                      "He goes to work.",
                      "She does her homework.",
                      "It has four wheels."
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "questionText": "Which is correct?"
              },
              "audioFile": ""
            },
